# Assets

Runtime is procedural terrain + authored GLBs/media/SFX. Binaries live under `public/assets/…` (Vite-served).

## Layout

```
public/assets/environments/sand/detail.png          # optional RGBA detail (512–1024)
public/assets/character/main_man.glb                # player skin + anims
public/assets/character/bow.glb                     # bow mesh (crush albedo)
public/assets/character/arrow.glb                   # flight + stuck arrows
public/assets/odyssey/models/*.glb                  # pillars, giant, antinous
public/assets/portfolio/org/*                       # edu/job logos only
public/assets/sfx/*.mp3                             # bow, impacts, giant/antinous VO
public/assets/boot/loading_screen_background.mp4    # boot loop
```

Env detail channels (match `detailBake`): RG = tangent normal XY (`n*0.5+0.5`), B = cavity, A = height. Missing → procedural bake. Sand-only: `PROFILES.snow.detailUrl = null` (no snow detail on disk).

## Size budget

- Keep `public/assets` lean (on the order of **~10MB** total after crush). Room exists for more, but only ship what loads at runtime.
- **Do not** commit unused portfolio project thumbs/GIFs — the pedestal card is text-only (`image: null` in `projects.json`).
- `scripts/syncPortfolio.mjs` syncs project **text** + org logos; it must not reintroduce project thumbs.
- Crush every new albedo GLB before commit (`node scripts/crushPillarTextures.mjs <path.glb>`).
- Prefer 512 detail maps / short muted boot loops / trimmed SFX over raw exports.

## Environments

- `S.environment` is the target (`snow` | `sand`); product default is sand.
- `envProfile.js` eases `envBlend`; systems call `getLerped()` — do not hard-swap mid-frame or clear the deform buffer.
- Do not rewrite spray for env switches — only tint/scale via profile.

## GLB pipeline

- Prop/player shading samples **albedo only**. Crush drops extra maps, max edge **512**, JPEG.
- New Meshy clips: merge animation accessors into the target GLB by **shared node indices**, then re-crush.
- CPU-skin skinned props (`computeBonesUsingShaders = false`) so `prop` / `staticDepth` / `staticPrepass` stay rigid shaders.

## Audio

- Use `src/combat/sfx.js` (`preloadSfx` / `playSfx` / `unlockAudio`) — Web Audio, no per-frame alloc.
- Trim leading silence from one-shots before commit (impact timing must match gameplay).
- Keep clips small: **mono ~22 kHz / 64 kbps MP3** is enough for SFX (avoid 256–320 kbps masters).
- Unlock on pointer-lock click / first shot.

## Boot

- `#boot` = looping muted video + progress bar + phase text only (no brand/title wordmark).
- Phase copy is thematic (dunes/walker/pillars); weights live in `main.js` `loading.phase(...)`.

## Git

`.gitignore` ignores binaries by default; allow via `!public/assets/{environments,character,portfolio,odyssey,boot,sfx}/…` exceptions. Keep large sources out until crushed.

## Rules

- Load behind loading phases; loaders next to the consumer — not dumped into `main.js`.
- Prefer authored when present; do not bake and authored for the same slot.
